  "description_short": "Country cafe on the R102 serving home-style meals, local produce, and friendly hospitality near Storms River.",
  "description_long": "Oudebosch Country Cafe sits along the scenic R102 between Storms River and Humansdorp, offering travellers a genuine taste of Tsitsikamma hospitality. The cafe specialises in hearty country cooking with an emphasis on fresh, local ingredients — think generous farm breakfasts, homemade soups, and traditional South African favourites that fuel your Garden Route adventure.\n\nThe setting is relaxed and welcoming, with a country charm that makes it easy to linger over coffee and cake. Beyond the kitchen, Oudebosch serves as a helpful stop for tour information and local tips, making it particularly popular with visitors exploring the Storms River area. Whether you're breaking up a long drive or looking for honest comfort food in a no-fuss environment, this roadside gem delivers exactly what you need.\n\nThe cafe's reputation for friendly service and consistent quality has made it a favourite pit stop for both tourists and locals. It's the kind of place where portion sizes are generous, the atmosphere is unpretentious, and you leave feeling looked after.",
